  "id": "index-of-validity",
  "term": "index of validity",
  "definition": "In psychological assessment, an index of validity is a measure used as a comparison standard to help judge whether another test or scale is valid. In the study packet, the Calgary Depression Scale for Schizophrenia served this role when evaluating the WHO-5.",
